SUMMARY:Commissioners' session (public comment at the start): Tarrow County
  vote on a 12-month battery storage pause (Res. 2026-118)
DESCRIPTION:Commissioners will take up Resolution 2026-118 at their October
  13 regular session. It would stop the county from accepting or processing
  zoning permits\, rezonings (zoning map amendments) and conditional use re
 quests for battery energy storage facilities of 1 MW or more for 12 months
 . It covers the areas under county zoning\, currently Ferris\, Quill and B
 rindle townships\; townships that run their own zoning are not affected. A
 pplications filed and found complete before it takes effect\, and batterie
 s that serve a single home or business on the same property\, are excluded
 .\n\nSource: Tarrow County Board of Commissioners\, agenda for October 13\
 , 2026 (PDF)\, page 2\, item 7\nhttps://www.tarrowcounty.example/commissio
 ners/agendas/2026-10-13-agenda.pdf\n\nFrom Battery Storage Zoning Watch\, 
 Week 41 (Fieldline Briefs). Check the official source before you rely on t
 his date. Not legal advice.
URL:https://www.tarrowcounty.example/commissioners/agendas/2026-10-13-agend
 a.pdf
CATEGORIES:Moratoria
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Commissioners' Chambers\, Tarrow County Administration Building\, 
 41 Court Street\, Tarrow City
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Reminder: Commissioners' session (public comment at the start)
TRIGGER:-P1D
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
