SUMMARY:Written comments due to the Zoning Inspector: Wrenfield Township ba
 ttery storage rules (ZTA-2026-03)
DESCRIPTION:Zoning text amendment ZTA-2026-03 would add definitions for bat
 tery energy storage systems and allow battery energy storage facilities on
 ly as a conditional use in the I-1 Light Industrial district. It would req
 uire setbacks of at least 300 feet from existing homes and 100 feet from p
 roperty lines\, a decommissioning plan backed by a bond or letter of credi
 t and reviewed every five years\, and a fire-safety plan reviewed by the f
 ire chief before a zoning certificate is issued.\n\nSource: Wrenfield Town
 ship\, notice of public hearing on ZTA-2026-03 (PDF)\, proposed amendments
  1 to 5\nhttps://www.wrenfieldtwp.example/notices/ZTA-2026-03-hearing-noti
 ce.pdf\n\nFrom Battery Storage Zoning Watch\, Week 41 (Fieldline Briefs). 
 Check the official source before you rely on this date. Not legal advice.
URL:https://www.wrenfieldtwp.example/notices/ZTA-2026-03-hearing-notice.pdf
CATEGORIES:Zoning rules
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Reminder: Written comments due to the Zoning Inspector
TRIGGER:-P1D
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
