UID:battery-storage-zoning-watch-w41-05-d954f97d99@fieldline.example
DTSTAMP:20261007T102627Z
DTSTART:20261019T230000Z
DTEND:20261020T000000Z
SUMMARY:City council second reading: Marlowe Falls battery fire-safety ordi
 nance (No. 2026-41)
DESCRIPTION:The Safety Committee amended Ordinance 2026-41 on October 5. As
  amended\, it applies to battery energy storage systems larger than 600 kW
 h (up from 50 kWh)\, other than systems serving a single one- or two-famil
 y home. It requires compliance with NFPA 855\, an emergency response plan 
 approved by the fire chief before a certificate of occupancy is issued\, a
  site walkthrough with the fire department once a year (down from twice a 
 year) and a 24-hour emergency contact posted at each entrance.\n\nSource: 
 City of Marlowe Falls\, Ordinance 2026-41 as amended (PDF)\, sections 1 to
  5\; committee amendments on page 2\nhttps://www.marlowefalls.example/coun
 cil/legislation/ord-2026-41-amended.pdf\n\nFrom Battery Storage Zoning Wat
 ch\, Week 41 (Fieldline Briefs). Check the official source before you rely
  on this date. Not legal advice.
URL:https://www.marlowefalls.example/council/legislation/ord-2026-41-amende
 d.pdf
CATEGORIES:Ordinances
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Council Chambers\, Marlowe Falls City Hall\, 12 Main Street
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Reminder: City council second reading
TRIGGER:-P1D
